    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added per-country national-number length validation to `normalizeTelephone` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`. After the existing E.164 normalization (which produces a `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits), the method now checks the national-number length against the country code:\n\n- **`+61`** (Australia) requires exactly **9** national digits\n- **`+1`** (NANP) requires exactly **10** national digits\n\nWhen the length is wrong for the recognized country code, it throws `InvalidTelephoneException`, which `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps to a **400 Bad Request**.\n\nKey points:\n- The check runs after the general 8\u201315 digit guard, and only fires for recognized country codes (`61`/`1` prefixes), so unrecognized codes keep the permissive 8\u201315 behavior.\n- Extracted a small `requireNationalLength` helper to keep the two cases DRY and produce a clear per-country error message.\n- The valid baseline payload (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 national digits) and the `+1` NANP seed data (10 national digits) both still pass, while the new acceptance test `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (`+61 123`) correctly gets a 400.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests pass.",
